I'm building a mobile website for spaza shops (South African informal grocery stores).

COMPLETED SO FAR:

Backend:
- Node.js + Express server
- SQLite database with better-sqlite3
- Session-based authentication for customers and merchants
- Multer for product photo uploads
- QR code generation (shop QR and order QR) using qrcode library
- Real barcode scanning with html5-qrcode (camera + manual fallback)

Database tables:
- customers (id, phone, email, password, saved_card)
- merchants (id, shop_name, phone, email, password, shop_address, owner_address, owner_photo, banking_details)
- products (id, barcode, name, price, picture, merchant_id)
- orders (id, customer_id, merchant_id, items JSON, total, status, order_qr)

Features working:
- Customer signup/login/logout
- Merchant signup/login/logout
- Merchant: add/edit/delete products with photo upload
- Merchant: view shop QR code (download/print)
- Merchant: verify orders by scanning order QR, see items, release customer
- Merchant: analytics dashboard (revenue, top products, daily sales, recent orders)
- Customer: scan shop QR (manual entry for prototype)
- Customer: scan product barcodes (camera or manual)
- Customer: shopping cart with add/remove
- Customer: fake payment checkout with order QR popup
- Customer: order history with status tracking

Styling:
- Mobile-friendly CSS
- Theme colors: #FFD700 (gold/yellow) as accent, black text, white background
- No emojis in text
- Product images shown in cart, order history, merchant verify, merchant products (70x70px)
- Loading spinners on async operations

